     "neutralisation",
     "antacid",
     "sour"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Lemon, tamarind and vinegar are acidic and taste sour. Soap, baking soda and toothpaste are basic and feel slippery.\nA base can cancel the effect of an acid. This is neutralisation. A bee sting is acidic so baking soda soothes it, while a wasp sting is basic and vinegar helps.\nIndigestion is eased by an antacid, which is a mild base."
    }
